      "params": {
        "text": "**CONTINUOUS PROJECTION PRINTING**\nReported: synchronized masks + continuous Z remove layer dead time.\nSource: 800 nm, 65 fs, 5 kHz and ~22 nm bandwidth.\n\n**TRY:** switch the laser off; rotate HWP from 0° to 22.5°;\ndisable DMD dispersion; freeze the mask or change ON fraction.\n**LIMIT:** geometric imaging; no temporal field, dose or curing.",
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fill": "#3e4c53"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "somers-interpretation-note",
      "type": "textlabel",
      "x": 55,
      "y": 350,
      "rot": 0,
      "params": {
        "text": "**FREE INTERPRETATION — NOT SPECIFIED IN THE PAPER**\n0.10 W display source power; 4.5 mm input beam; 5 mW alignment;\ncompact fold and relay placement; DMD carrier 92.6 lines/mm, order 5;\n0.4 Hz masks; 0.1 mm stage travel; objective EFL/WD/transmission;\ndisplay resin properties. The preview clock is not controller timing.\n\n**OBSERVATION PATH LIMIT**\nThe paper describes CCD imaging of the sample through the objective.\nThis branch measures incident writing/alignment light only;\nno reflected sample image or return illumination is computed.\nThe 633 nm alignment source is optional and starts disabled.",
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fill": "#7a4b18"
